# Without this file the Dockerfiles are wrong on any machine that has run
# `npm install`. Both of them do `COPY --from=deps /repo/node_modules` and then
# `COPY . .`, so an un-ignored host `node_modules` lands on top of the one the
# image just resolved — carrying the host's platform-specific binaries (esbuild,
# rollup) into a linux/amd64 image, where they fail to load. NFR-36 says a clean
# machine, and a clean machine would have worked; every developer's machine
# would not.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output is produced inside the image. Copying the host's in only risks
# shipping something staler than what was just compiled.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build

# Turborepo and Vite caches: large, machine-local, and meaningless in the image.
.turbo
**/.turbo
.vite
**/.vite

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets stay out of the image. The api reads them at runtime via
# `env_file: .env` in docker-compose.yml, which is a mount, not a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor and agent scratch space.
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# Documentation does not change the built artifact. `assets/` deliberately stays
# in: the api both reads the Map Document and serves the directory statically.
docs
specs
*.md
!README.md
